<title>ITALY: Zalm and Ciampi to discuss EMU, budget discipline.</title>
<headline>Zalm and Ciampi to discuss EMU, budget discipline.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Finance Minister Gerrit Zalm and Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi will talk about the launch of the single European currency and reinforcing European Union budget discipline, a Treasury source said.</p>
<p>Zalm and Ciampi are having lunch together and are expected to issue a joint statement later on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Treasury source said the statement was expected to reiterate both countries' commitment to the present timetable for European economic and monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>Zalm is scheduled to catch a flight back home at 4.30 p.m. (1530 GMT). No news conference is scheduled.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
